		⟪(b)⟫ c. ptcp. pr. (esp. in impf., as in Heb. and Aram.; Dalman, Words, 35 f.), ⟦Matthew 7:29|Mt 7:29⟧, ⟦Mark 1:22|Mk 1:22⟧, ⟦Luke 4:31|Lk 4:31⟧ ⟦Luke 14:1|14:1⟧, ⟦Acts 1:10|Ac 1:10⟧, al. mult., id. for imper. (M, Pr., 180f., 182f.), with ellipsis of εἰμί, ⟦Romans 12:9|Ro 12:9⟧, ⟦Romans 12:10|10⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:5|He 13:5⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ c. ptcp. aor. (cl), ⟦Luke 23:9|Lk 23:9⟧.
	⟪6.⟫ Seq. εἰς (cf. Heb. ⁨הָיָה לְ⁩), a vernac. usage (M, Pr., 71): ⟦Matthew 19:5|Mt 19:5⟧, ⟦Mark 10:8|Mk 10:8⟧, ⟦Hebrews 8:10|He 8:10⟧, al.
	⟪7.⟫ C. adv.: ⟦Matthew 19:20|Mt 19:20⟧, ⟦Mark 4:26|Mk 4:26⟧, ⟦Luke 18:11|Lk 18:11⟧, al.
	⟪8.⟫ Ellipses;
		⟪(a)⟫ of the copula (Bl., §30, 3): ⟦Matthew 8:29|Mt 8:29⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:32|24:32⟧, ⟦John 21:22|Jo 21:22⟧, ⟦John 21:23|23⟧, ⟦Hebrews 6:4|He 6:4⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ of the predicate: ἐγώ εἰμί, ⟦Matthew 14:27|Mt 14:27⟧, ⟦Mark 6:50|Mk 6:50⟧, al.; absol. (cf. ⟦Deuteronomy 32:39|De 32:39⟧; ⁨אֲנִי הוּא⁩), ⟦Mark 13:6|Mk 13:6⟧, ⟦John 4:26|Jo 4:26⟧, al. (cf. ἄπ-, ἔν-, πάρ-, συμ-πάρ-, σύν-ειμι).

G1519.b:
⟪εἰς⟫, prep. c. acc., expressing entrance, direction, limit, ⟪into, unto, to, upon, towards, for, among⟫ (Lat. in, c. acc.).
⟪I.⟫ Of place.
	⟪1.⟫ After verbs of motion;
		⟪(a)⟫ of entrance into: ⟦Matthew 8:23|Mt 8:23⟧ ⟦Matthew 9:7|9:7⟧, ⟦Mark 1:45|Mk 1:45⟧, ⟦Luke 2:15|Lk 2:15⟧ ⟦Luke 8:31|8:31⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ of approach, ⟪to⟫ or ⟪towards⟫: ⟦Mark 11:1|Mk 11:1⟧, ⟦Luke 6:8|Lk 6:8⟧ ⟦Luke 19:28|19:28⟧, ⟦John 11:31|Jo 11:31⟧ ⟦John 21:6|21:6⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ before pl. and collective nouns, ⟪among⟫: ⟦Mark 4:7|Mk 4:7⟧ ⟦Mark 8:19|8:19⟧, ⟦Mark 8:20|20⟧, ⟦Luke 11:49|Lk 11:49⟧, ⟦John 21:23|Jo 21:23⟧, al.;
		⟪(d)⟫ Of a limit reached, ⟪unto, on, upon⟫: ⟦Matthew 8:18|Mt 8:18⟧, ⟦Matthew 21:1|21:1⟧, ⟦Mark 11:1|Mk 11:1⟧ ⟦Mark 13:16|13:16⟧, ⟦Luke 14:10|Lk 14:10⟧, ⟦John 6:3|Jo 6:3⟧ ⟦John 11:32|11:32⟧, al.; c. acc. pers. (as in Ep. and Ion.), ⟦Acts 23:15|Ac 23:15⟧, ⟦Romans 5:12|Ro 5:12⟧ ⟦Romans 16:19|16:19⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:14|II Co 10:14⟧;
		⟪(e)⟫ elliptical: ἐπιστολαὶ εἰς Δαμασκόν, ⟦Acts 9:2|Ac 9:2⟧; ἡ διακονία μου ἡ εἰς Ἱ., ⟦Romans 15:31|Ro 15:31⟧; metaph., of entrance into a certain state or condition, or of approach or direction towards some end (Thayer, B, i, 1; ii, 1), εἰς τ. ὄνομα, M, Pr., 200.
	⟪2.⟫ Of direction;
		⟪(a)⟫ after verbs of seeing: ⟦Matthew 6:26|Mt 6:26⟧, ⟦Mark 6:41|Mk 6:41⟧, ⟦Luke 9:16|Lk 9:16⟧, ⟦Luke 9:62|62⟧, ⟦John 13:22|Jo 13:22⟧, al.; metaph., of the mind, ⟦Hebrews 11:26|He 11:26⟧ ⟦Hebrews 12:2|12:2⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ after verbs of speaking: ⟦Matthew 13:10|Mt 13:10⟧ ⟦Matthew 14:9|14:9⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:9|I Th 2:9⟧, al.
	⟪3.⟫ After verbs of rest;
		⟪(a)⟫ in "pregnant" construction, implying previous motion (cl.; v. WM, 516; Bl., §39, 3; M, Pr., 234f.): ⟦Matthew 2:23|Mt 2:23⟧ ⟦Matthew 4:13|4:13⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:4|II Th 2:4⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:11|II Ti 1:11⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:9|He 11:9⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ by an assimilation general in late Gk (v. Bl., M, Pr., ll. c.) = ἐν: ⟦Luke 1:44|Lk 1:44⟧ ⟦Luke 4:23|4:23⟧, ⟦Acts 20:16|Ac 20:16⟧ ⟦Acts 21:17|21:17⟧, ⟦John 1:18|Jo 1:18⟧ (but v. Westc, in l.), al.
⟪II.⟫ Of time, ⟪for, unto⟫;
	⟪1.⟫ accentuating the duration expressed by the acc.: εἰς τ. αἰῶνα, ⟦Matthew 21:19|Mt 21:19⟧; εἰς γενεὰς καὶ γ., ⟦Luke 1:50|Lk 1:50⟧; εἰς τ. διηνεκές, ⟦Hebrews 7:3|He 7:3⟧, al.
	⟪2.⟫ Of a point or limit of time, ⟪unto, up to, until⟫: ⟦Matthew 6:34|Mt 6:34⟧, ⟦Acts 4:3|Ac 4:3⟧ ⟦Acts 25:21|25:21⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:10|Phl 1:10⟧ ⟦Philippians 2:16|2:16⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:15|I Th 4:15⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:12|II Ti 1:12⟧; of entrance into a future period, εις τὸ μέλλον (v.s. μέλλω), ⟪next (year)⟫, ⟦Luke 13:9|Lk 13:9⟧ (but c. ICC, in l.); εἰς τ. μεταξὺ σάββατον, ⟪on the next Sabbath⟫, ⟦Acts 13:42|Ac 13:42⟧; εἰς τὸ πάλιν (v.s. πάλιν, ⟦2 Corinthians 13:2|II Co 13:2⟧.
⟪III.⟫ Of result, after verbs of changing, joining, dividing, etc.: στρέφειν εἰς, ⟦Revelation 11:6|Re 11:6⟧; μετας-, ⟦Acts 2:20|Ac 2:20⟧, ⟦James 4:9|Ja 4:9⟧; μεταλλάσσειν, ⟦Romans 1:26|Ro 1:26⟧; σχίζειν εἰς δύο, ⟦Matthew 27:51|Mt 27:51⟧, al.; predicatively with εἴναι, ⟦Acts 8:23|Ac 8:23⟧.
⟪IV.⟫ Of relation, ⟪to, towards, for, in regard to⟫ (so in cl., but more freq. in late Gk., εἰς encroaching on the simple dat., which it has wholly displaced in MGr.; Jannaris, Gr., §1541; Robertson, Gr., 594; Deiss., BS, 117f.): ⟦Luke 7:30|Lk 7:30⟧, ⟦Romans 4:20|Ro 4:20⟧ ⟦Romans 15:2|15:2⟧, ⟦Romans 15:26|26⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:1|I Co 16:1⟧, ⟦Ephesians 3:16|Eph 3:16⟧, al.; ἀγάπη εἰς, ⟦Romans 5:8|Ro 5:8⟧, al.; χρηστός, ⟦Ephesians 4:32|Eph 4:32⟧; φρονεῖν εἰς, ⟦Romans 12:16|Ro 12:16⟧; θαρρεῖν, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:1|II Co 10:1⟧.
⟪V.⟫ Of the end or object: εὔθετος εἰς, ⟦Luke 14:34|Lk 14:34⟧; σόφος, ⟦Romans 16:19|Ro 16:19⟧; ἰσχύειν, ⟦Matthew 5:13|Mt 5:13⟧; εἰς τοῦτο, ⟦Mark 1:38|Mk 1:38⟧, al.; ἀφορίζειν εἰς, ⟦Romans 1:1|Ro 1:1⟧; indicating purpose, εἰς φόβον, ⟦Romans 8:15|Ro 8:15⟧; εἰς ἔνδειξιν, ⟦Romans 3:25|Ro 3:25⟧; εἰς τό, c. inf. (= ἵνα or ὥστε; Bl., §71, 5; M, Pr., 218ff.): ⟦Matthew 20:19|Mt 20:19⟧, ⟦Romans 1:11|Ro 1:11⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:18|I Co 9:18⟧, al.
⟪VI.⟫ Adverbial phrases: εἰς τέλος, εἰς τὸ πάλιν, etc (v.s. τέλος, πάλιν, etc.).

G1520.b:
⟪εἷς⟫, μιά, ἕν, gen. ἑνός, μιᾶς, ἑνός, cardinal numeral, ⟪one⟫;
⟪1.⟫ ⟪one⟫, as opp. to many: ⟦Matthew 25:15|Mt 25:15⟧, ⟦Romans 5:12|Ro 5:12⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:8|I Co 10:8⟧, al.; as subst., ⟦Romans 5:15|Ro 5:15⟧, ⟦Ephesians 2:14|Eph 2:14⟧; id. c. gen. partit., ⟦Matthew 5:19|Mt 5:19⟧, al.; seq. ἐκ (ἐξ), ⟦Mark 14:18|Mk 14:18⟧, ⟦John 6:8|Jo 6:8⟧, al.; metaph., of union and concord, ⟦John 10:30|Jo 10:30⟧ ⟦John 17:11|17:11⟧, ⟦Romans 12:4|Ro 12:4⟧, ⟦Romans 12:5|5⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:27|Phl 1:27⟧; ἀπὸ μιᾶς (B1., § 44, 1), ⟦Luke 14:18|Lk 14:18⟧; c. neg., εἷς. . . οὐ (μή), more emphatic than οὐδείς, no one, none (cl.), ⟦Matthew 5:18|Mt 5:18⟧ ⟦Matthew 10:29|10:29⟧, ⟦Luke 11:46|Lk 11:46⟧ ⟦Luke 12:6|12:6⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Emphati­cally, to the exclusion of others;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a single (one)⟫: ⟦Matthew 21:24|Mt 21:24⟧, ⟦Mark 8:14|Mk 8:14⟧; absol., ⟦1 Corinthians 9:24|I Co 9:24⟧, al.; οὐδὲ εἷς, ⟦Matthew 27:14|Mt 27:14⟧, ⟦John 1:3|Jo 1:3⟧, ⟦Romans 3:10|Ro 3:10⟧, al.;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪one, alone⟫: ⟦Mark 2:7|Mk 2:7⟧ ⟦Mark 10:18|10:18⟧, ⟦Luke 18:19|Lk 18:19⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪one and the same⟫: ⟦Romans 3:30|Ro 3:30⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:8|I Co 3:8⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 11:5|11:5⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 12:11|12:11⟧, ⟦1 John 5:8|I Jo 5:8⟧.
⟪3.⟫ In late Gk., with weakened force, = τις or indef. art. (of. Heb. ⁨אֶחָד⁩, ⟦Genesis 22:13|Ge 22:13⟧, al.; v. B1., § 45, 2; M, Pr., 96 f.): ⟦Matthew 8:19|Mt 8:19⟧ ⟦Matthew 19:6|19:6⟧, ⟦Revelation 8:13|Re 8:13⟧, al.; εἷς τις (Bl., l.c.), ⟦Luke 22:50|Lk 22:50⟧, ⟦John 11:49|Jo 11:49⟧
⟪4.⟫ Distributively: εἷς καστος (cl.), ⟦Luke 4:40|Lk 4:40⟧, ⟦Acts 2:6|Ac 2:6⟧, al.; εἷς . . . καὶ εἷς (cl., εἷς μὲν . . . εἷς δέ), ⟦Matthew 17:4|Mt 17:4⟧, ⟦Mark 9:5|Mk 9:5⟧, ⟦John 20:12|Jo 20:12⟧, al. (cf. LXX and use of Heb. ⁨אֶחָד⁩, ⟦Exodus 17:12|Ex 17:12⟧, al); ὁ εἷς . . . ὁ ἕτερος (ἄλλος) = cl. ὁ μὲν (ἕτερος) . . . ὁ δέ (ἕτερος), ⟦Matthew 6:24|Mt 6:24⟧, ⟦Luke 7:41|Lk 7:41⟧, ⟦Revelation 17:10|Re 17:10⟧; καθ’ εἷς, εἷς κ. είς (in which καθ’ is adverbial, or the expression formed from the analogy of ἕν καθ’ ἔν; M, Pr., 105), one by one, severally: ⟦Mark 14:19|Mk 14:19⟧, ⟦Romans 12:5|Ro 12:5⟧, al.; εἷς τὸν ἕνα = ἀλλήλους (B1., 45, 2; M, Pr., 246), ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:11|I Th 5:11⟧.
⟪5.⟫ As ordinal = πρῶτος (like Heb. ⁨אֶחָד⁩; Bl., § 45, 1; M, Pr., 95 f.), first: ⟦Matthew 28:1|Mt 28:1⟧, ⟦Mark 16:2|Mk 16:2⟧, al.

G1534.b:
⟪εἶτα⟫ adv., denoting sequence;
⟪1.⟫ of time; ⟪then, next⟫: ⟦Mark 8:25|Mk 8:25⟧, ⟦Luke 8:12|Lk 8:12⟧, ⟦John 13:5|Jo 13:5⟧ ⟦John 19:27|19:27⟧ ⟦John 20:27|20:27⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:10|I Ti 3:10⟧, ⟦James 1:15|Ja 1:15⟧; seq. gen. abs., ⟦Mark 4:17|Mk 4:17⟧; in enumerations, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:5|I Co 15:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:7|7⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:24|24⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 2:13|I Ti 2:13⟧.
⟪2.⟫ In argument;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪therefore, then⟫,
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪furthermore⟫: ⟦Hebrews 12:9|He 12:9⟧ (cf. εἶτεν).†

G1538.b:
* ⟪ἕκαστος⟫, -η, ὂν, [in LXX chiefly for ⁨אִישׁ⁩;] ⟪each, every⟫ (Lat. quisque) ;
⟪(a)⟫ with a noun: ⟦Luke 6:44|Lk 6:44⟧, ⟦John 19:23|Jo 19:23⟧, seq. κατά, ⟦Hebrews 3:13|He 3:13⟧, ⟦Revelation 22:2|Re 22:2⟧; εἷς ἕ., ⟦Ephesians 4:16|Eph 4:16⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ without a noun: ⟦Acts 4:35|Ac 4:35⟧, ⟦Romans 2:6|Ro 2:6⟧, al.;
⟪(c)⟫ partit. gen., ⟦Romans 14:12|Ro 14:12⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:12|I Co 1:12⟧, al.; in sing, with pl. verb, ⟦Luke 2:3|Lk 2:3⟧, ⟦Acts 11:29|Ac 11:29⟧, al.; in apposition with pl. noun or pron., ⟦Luke 2:3|Lk 2:3⟧, ⟦John 16:32|Jo 16:32⟧, ⟦Acts 2:8|Ac 2:8⟧ ⟦Acts 3:26|3:26⟧, al.; εἷς ἕ. (Lat. unusquisque), ⟦Acts 2:6|Ac 2:6⟧ ⟦Acts 21:26|21:26⟧, ⟦Colossians 4:6|Col 4:6⟧, al; ἕ. τι ἀδελφῷ (= Heb. ⁨אִישׁ לְאָחִיו⁩, ⟦Genesis 26:31|Ge 26:31⟧), ⟦Matthew 18:35|Mt 18:35⟧ (cf. ⟦Hebrews 8:11|He 8:11⟧); ἕ. μετὰ τοῦ πλησίον (= ⁨אִישׁ אֶל־רֵעֵהוּ⁩, ⟦Judges 6:29|Jg 6:29⟧, al.), ⟦Ephesians 4:25|Eph 4:25⟧.

G1561.b:
* ⟪ἐκ-δοχή -ῆς⟫, ἡ
(< ἐκδέχομαι);
⟪1.⟫ in cl.,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a receiving from, succession⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪an interpretation⟫.
⟪2.⟫ In NT, = προσδοκία, ⟪expectation⟫: ⟦Hebrews 10:27|He 10:27⟧ (cf. Field, Notes, 231; Cremer, 688).†

G1577.b:
⟪ἐκκλησία⟫, -ας, ἡ
(< ἐκ-καλέω), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨קָהָל⁩, otherwise for one of its cogn. forms ;]
⟪1.⟫ prop., ⟪an assembly⟫ of citizens regularly convened (in Thuc., ii, 22, opp. to σύλλογος, a concourse): ⟦Acts 19:32|Ac 19:32⟧, ⟦Acts 19:39|39⟧, ⟦Acts 19:41|41⟧.
⟪2.⟫ In LXX of ⟪the assembly, congregation, community⟫ of Israel (De 4:10 23:2, al.): ⟦Acts 7:38|Ac 7:38⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:12|He 2:12⟧ (LXX).
⟪3.⟫ NT, esp. of an assembly or company of Christians, a ⟪(the) church⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of gatherings for worship: ⟦1 Corinthians 11:18|I Co 11:18⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 14:19|14:19⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:34|34⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:35|35⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of local communities: ⟦Acts 8:3|Ac 8:3⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:17|I Co 4:17⟧; with name added, ⟦Acts 8:1|Ac 8:1⟧, ⟦Romans 16:1|Ro 16:1⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 1:1|I Th 1:1⟧, al.; pl., ⟦Acts 15:41|Ac 15:41⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:17|I Co 7:17⟧; τ. Χριστοῦ, ⟦Romans 16:16|Ro 16:16⟧; τ. Ἀσίας, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:19|I Co 16:19⟧; τ. ἁγίων, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:33|I Co 14:33⟧; εἰπὸν τ. ἐκκλησίᾳ, ⟦Matthew 18:17|Mt 18:17⟧ (but v. Hort, Ecclesia, 10); of a house-congregation (DB, i, 431a), ⟦Romans 16:5|Ro 16:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:19|I Co 16:19⟧, ⟦Colossians 4:15|Col 4:15⟧, ⟦Philemon 1:2|Phm 2⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of the whole body of Christians: ⟦Matthew 16:18|Mt 16:18⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:28|I Co 12:28⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:22|Eph 1:22⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:6|Phl 3:6⟧, al.; τ. θεοῦ, ⟦Acts 20:28|Ac 20:28⟧ (Κυρίου, T, R, mg.), ⟦1 Corinthians 15:9|I Co 15:9⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:13|Ga 1:13⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:15|I Ti 3:15⟧; ἐ. προτοτόκων ἀπογεγραμμένων ἐν οὐρανοῖς, ⟦Hebrews 12:23|He 12:23⟧.
SYN.: συναγωγή, q.v. (v. Tr., Syn., §i; DB, i, 426; Hort, Ecclesia, esp. 4ff., 107ff.; Hamilton, People of God, ii, 37ff.; reff. s.vv. "Church," "Congregation," in DB and DCG; Cremer, 332).

G1588.b:
⟪ἐκ-λεκτός, -ή, -όν⟫
(< ἐκλέγω), [in LXX for ⁨בָּחַר⁩ (so prob. in ⟦Isaiah 28:16|Is 28:16⟧, ⟦Proverbs 17:3|Pr 17:3⟧, for MT ⁨בָּחַן⁩), ⁨בָּרִיא⁩, etc. ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪choice, select⟫ (cl., rarely; Thuc., Plat., al.), hence, ⟪eminent⟫: ⟦Romans 16:13|Ro 16:13⟧ (cf. ⟦Ezekiel 27:24|Ez 27:24⟧).
⟪2.⟫ As in Inscr. (MM, Exp., xii), ⟪chosen⟫; esp. as in LXX, of Israel, ⟪elect, chosen⟫of God (⟦Isaiah 65:9|Is 65:9⟧, ⟦Psalms 105:43|Ps 105:43⟧, al.); so in NT;
⟪(a)⟫ of Christ: ⟦Luke 23:35|Lk 23:35⟧ (cf. ⟦Isaiah 42:1|Is 42:1⟧); fig., λίθος, ⟦1 Peter 2:4|I Pe 2:4⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:6|6⟧ (LXX);
⟪(b)⟫ of holy angels: ⟦1 Timothy 5:21|I Ti 5:21⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of Christians: ⟦Matthew 24:22|Mt 24:22⟧, ⟦Matthew 24:24|24⟧, ⟦Mark 13:20|Mk 13:20⟧, ⟦Mark 13:22|22⟧, ⟦Mark 13:27|27⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 2:10|II Ti 2:10⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:1|I Pe 1:1⟧; τ. θεοῦ, ⟦Luke 18:7|Lk 18:7⟧, ⟦Romans 8:33|Ro 8:33⟧, ⟦Colossians 3:12|Col 3:12⟧, ⟦Titus 1:1|Tit 1:1⟧; τ. Χριστοῦ, ⟦Matthew 24:31|Mt 24:31⟧; ἐ. κυρία, ⟦2 John 1:1|II Jo 1⟧; ἀδελφή, ⟦2 John 1:13|ib. 13⟧; γένος, ⟦1 Peter 2:9|I Pe 2:9⟧ (LXX); κλητοὶ καὶ ἐ. κ. πιστοί, ⟦Revelation 17:14|Re 17:14⟧; opp. to κλητός (not so in Epp.; v. Lft. on ⟦Colossians 3:12|Col 3:12⟧), ⟦Matthew 20:16|Mt 20:16⟧ (T, WH, txt., R, omit) ⟦Matthew 22:14|Mt 22:14⟧ (Cremer, 405, 775).†
